window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b342-5b26128f06b7ea7e.json"]={sha256:"5b26128f06b7ea7e984a3c951a6b523ce0ef346ebbcfff39a050e4048ca06914",value:{"id":"b342","title":"鋼軌鋁熱焊接","titleEn":"Aluminothermic rail welding","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"鋼軌鋁熱焊接以「現場接頭熱量收縮形貌與無損檢測」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。鋁熱焊課程只分析接頭能量、凝固收縮與焊後驗證；化學配方、點火及現場操作均不由教學模型指定，重點是辨認外觀與內部品質的差異。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops field-joint heat shrinkage profile and nondestructive inspection through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. This aluminothermic-weld course analyses joint energy, solidification shrinkage and post-weld verification; it specifies no chemical recipe, ignition or field procedure, and distinguishes visible profile from internal quality. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["焊接材料","Welding material"],["熱量收支","Heat balance"],["接頭凝固","Joint solidification"],["幾何整修","Geometry finishing"],["品質取證","Quality evidence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["焊接材料","熱量收支","接頭凝固","幾何整修","品質取證"],"labelsEn":["Welding material","Heat balance","Joint solidification","Geometry finishing","Quality evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=6.864 kg。模型邊界：有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=1650 kJ。模型邊界：給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.864 kg. Boundary: Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=1650 kJ. Boundary: Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b342-v16-s1","title":"接頭金屬質量與接頭顯熱量級","titleEn":"Joint metal mass & Joint sensible-heat scale","description":"本階段聚焦「接頭金屬質量」與「接頭顯熱量級」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Joint metal mass\" and \"Joint sensible-heat scale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b342-v16-01","title":"接頭金屬質量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint metal mass: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「接頭金屬質量」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint metal mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"密度乘有效體積可核對材料帳，外部餘料需分開。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.864 kg。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料。使用接頭幾何與有效體積作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接頭金屬質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Density times effective volume checks the material account, keeping external surplus separate. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 6.864 kg. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded. Use joint geometry and effective volume as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint metal mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接頭金屬質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint metal mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-01-k1","title":"接頭金屬質量","titleEn":"Joint metal mass","text":"密度乘有效體積可核對材料帳，外部餘料需分開。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 6.864 kg。","textEn":"Density times effective volume checks the material account, keeping external surplus separate. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭金屬質量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint metal mass\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量","密度乘有效體積可核對材料帳，外部餘料需分開。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill.","Density times effective volume checks the material account, keeping external surplus separate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"密度乘有效體積可核對材料帳，外部餘料需分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Density times effective volume checks the material account, keeping external surplus separate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b342-v16-02","title":"接頭金屬質量：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint metal mass: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接頭金屬質量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint metal mass” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=6.864 kg。模型邊界：有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.864 kg. Boundary: Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以接頭幾何與有效體積區分模型與觀察，先用接頭模型三維體積、密度資料及獨立秤重建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use joint geometry and effective volume to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=6.864 kg。模型邊界：有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=6.864 kg. Boundary: Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭金屬質量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint metal mass\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3；y=rho*V=6.24 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=7800 kg/m3, V=0.0008 m3; y=rho*V=6.24 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b342-v16-03","title":"接頭金屬質量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint metal mass: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接頭金屬質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint metal mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以接頭幾何與有效體積區分模型與觀察，先用接頭模型三維體積、密度資料及獨立秤重建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接頭金屬質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use joint geometry and effective volume to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using three-dimensional joint-model volume, density data and independent weighing, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Joint metal mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接頭金屬質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量造成偏離的合成觀察，以接頭幾何與有效體積說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Joint metal mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. Explain which evidence in joint geometry and effective volume distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以接頭幾何與有效體積區分模型與觀察，先用接頭模型三維體積、密度資料及獨立秤重建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接頭金屬質量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use joint geometry and effective volume to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using three-dimensional joint-model volume, density data and independent weighing, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Joint metal mass. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接頭金屬質量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出有效體積與密度對應同一溫度狀態；不含外部餘料如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量造成偏離的合成觀察，以接頭幾何與有效體積說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Joint metal mass, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Effective volume and density refer to the same temperature state; external surplus is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. Explain which evidence in joint geometry and effective volume distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭金屬質量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint metal mass\"?","options":["本單元以接頭幾何與有效體積區分模型與觀察，先用接頭模型三維體積、密度資料及獨立秤重建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力"],"optionsEn":["Use joint geometry and effective volume to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以接頭幾何與有效體積區分模型與觀察，先用接頭模型三維體積、密度資料及獨立秤重建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use joint geometry and effective volume to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b342-v16-04","title":"接頭金屬質量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint metal mass: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接頭金屬質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint metal mass” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量。這個失效與「接頭金屬質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接頭幾何與有效體積，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. This failure and a measurement bias in Joint metal mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check joint geometry and effective volume rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用接頭幾何與有效體積作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量。這個失效與「接頭金屬質量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接頭幾何與有效體積，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. This failure and a measurement bias in Joint metal mass can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check joint geometry and effective volume rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭金屬質量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint metal mass\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b342-v16-05","title":"接頭顯熱量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint sensible-heat scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「接頭顯熱量級」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint sensible-heat scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"顯熱只描述溫度變化，凝固潛熱必須另列。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1650 kJ。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算。使用質量與溫度歷程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接頭顯熱量級」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sensible heat describes temperature change; latent heat of solidification is separate. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1650 kJ. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate. Use mass and temperature history as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint sensible-heat scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接頭顯熱量級」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint sensible-heat scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-05-k1","title":"接頭顯熱量級","titleEn":"Joint sensible-heat scale","text":"顯熱只描述溫度變化，凝固潛熱必須另列。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1650 kJ。","textEn":"Sensible heat describes temperature change; latent heat of solidification is separate. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接頭顯熱量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint sensible-heat scale\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應","顯熱只描述溫度變化，凝固潛熱必須另列。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","Sensible heat describes temperature change; latent heat of solidification is separate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"顯熱只描述溫度變化，凝固潛熱必須另列。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sensible heat describes temperature change; latent heat of solidification is separate. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b342-v16-06","title":"接頭顯熱量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint sensible-heat scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接頭顯熱量級」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint sensible-heat scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=1650 kJ。模型邊界：給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=1650 kJ. Boundary: Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以質量與溫度歷程區分模型與觀察，先用合成金屬溫度歷程、有效質量及熱容量紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use mass and temperature history to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=1650 kJ。模型邊界：給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=1650 kJ. Boundary: Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接頭顯熱量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint sensible-heat scale\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K；y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, c=600 J/kgK, dT=500 K; y=m*c*dT/1000=1500 kJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b342-v16-07","title":"接頭顯熱量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint sensible-heat scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接頭顯熱量級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint sensible-heat scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以質量與溫度歷程區分模型與觀察，先用合成金屬溫度歷程、有效質量及熱容量紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接頭顯熱量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use mass and temperature history to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic metal-temperature history, effective mass and heat-capacity records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Joint sensible-heat scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接頭顯熱量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以質量與溫度歷程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Joint sensible-heat scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. Explain which evidence in mass and temperature history distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以質量與溫度歷程區分模型與觀察，先用合成金屬溫度歷程、有效質量及熱容量紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接頭顯熱量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use mass and temperature history to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic metal-temperature history, effective mass and heat-capacity records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Joint sensible-heat scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接頭顯熱量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出給定金屬質量、定比熱及均勻溫升；相變潛熱另算如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間造成偏離的合成觀察，以質量與溫度歷程說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Joint sensible-heat scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Given metal mass, constant heat capacity and uniform temperature rise; phase-change latent heat is separate. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. Explain which evidence in mass and temperature history distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接頭顯熱量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint sensible-heat scale\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以質量與溫度歷程區分模型與觀察，先用合成金屬溫度歷程、有效質量及熱容量紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use mass and temperature history to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以質量與溫度歷程區分模型與觀察，先用合成金屬溫度歷程、有效質量及熱容量紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use mass and temperature history to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b342-v16-08","title":"接頭顯熱量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint sensible-heat scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接頭顯熱量級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint sensible-heat scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間。這個失效與「接頭顯熱量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查質量與溫度歷程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. This failure and a measurement bias in Joint sensible-heat scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check mass and temperature history rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用質量與溫度歷程作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間。這個失效與「接頭顯熱量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查質量與溫度歷程，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. This failure and a measurement bias in Joint sensible-heat scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check mass and temperature history rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接頭顯熱量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint sensible-heat scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應","忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b342-v16-s2","title":"凝固潛熱帳與體積收縮量","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account & Volume-shrinkage estimate","description":"本階段聚焦「凝固潛熱帳」與「體積收縮量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Solidification latent-heat account\" and \"Volume-shrinkage estimate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b342-v16-09","title":"凝固潛熱帳：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「凝固潛熱帳」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Solidification latent-heat account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相變放熱可以在溫度變化很小時持續發生。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1485 kJ。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。全部指定質量完成同一相變；潛熱視為常數。使用冷卻曲線平台作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「凝固潛熱帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Phase-change heat can be released while temperature changes little. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1485 kJ. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. The specified mass completes the same phase change; latent heat is constant. Use a plateau in the cooling trace as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solidification latent-heat account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=1350 kJ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=1350 kJ.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「凝固潛熱帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solidification latent-heat account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-09-k1","title":"凝固潛熱帳","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account","text":"相變放熱可以在溫度變化很小時持續發生。本模型把 m 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1485 kJ。","textEn":"Phase-change heat can be released while temperature changes little. In this model, m is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「凝固潛熱帳」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Solidification latent-heat account\" is correct?","options":["相變放熱可以在溫度變化很小時持續發生。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Phase-change heat can be released while temperature changes little.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相變放熱可以在溫度變化很小時持續發生。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Phase-change heat can be released while temperature changes little. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b342-v16-10","title":"凝固潛熱帳：定量估算","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「凝固潛熱帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Solidification latent-heat account” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=1350 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=1485 kJ。模型邊界：全部指定質量完成同一相變；潛熱視為常數；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=1350 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=1485 kJ. Boundary: The specified mass completes the same phase change; latent heat is constant; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以冷卻曲線平台區分模型與觀察，先用合成冷卻曲線、相變比例與熱量收支建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use a plateau in the cooling trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=1350 kJ。只把 m 增加百分之十，y=1485 kJ。模型邊界：全部指定質量完成同一相變；潛熱視為常數；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=1350 kJ. Increasing only m with a ten-percent increase gives y=1485 kJ. Boundary: The specified mass completes the same phase change; latent heat is constant; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「凝固潛熱帳」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Solidification latent-heat account\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=1350 kJ。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=1350 kJ.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg；y=m*latent=1350 kJ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: m=5 kg, latent=270 kJ/kg; y=m*latent=1350 kJ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b342-v16-11","title":"凝固潛熱帳：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「凝固潛熱帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solidification latent-heat account” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以冷卻曲線平台區分模型與觀察，先用合成冷卻曲線、相變比例與熱量收支建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「凝固潛熱帳」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use a plateau in the cooling trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic cooling trace, transformed fraction and heat balance, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Solidification latent-heat account. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「凝固潛熱帳」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全部指定質量完成同一相變；潛熱視為常數如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應造成偏離的合成觀察，以冷卻曲線平台說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Solidification latent-heat account, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: The specified mass completes the same phase change; latent heat is constant. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. Explain which evidence in a plateau in the cooling trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以冷卻曲線平台區分模型與觀察，先用合成冷卻曲線、相變比例與熱量收支建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「凝固潛熱帳」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use a plateau in the cooling trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic cooling trace, transformed fraction and heat balance, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Solidification latent-heat account. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「凝固潛熱帳」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出全部指定質量完成同一相變；潛熱視為常數如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應造成偏離的合成觀察，以冷卻曲線平台說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Solidification latent-heat account, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: The specified mass completes the same phase change; latent heat is constant. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. Explain which evidence in a plateau in the cooling trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「凝固潛熱帳」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Solidification latent-heat account\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符","本單元以冷卻曲線平台區分模型與觀察，先用合成冷卻曲線、相變比例與熱量收支建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.","Use a plateau in the cooling trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以冷卻曲線平台區分模型與觀察，先用合成冷卻曲線、相變比例與熱量收支建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use a plateau in the cooling trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b342-v16-12","title":"凝固潛熱帳：失效診斷","titleEn":"Solidification latent-heat account: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「凝固潛熱帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Solidification latent-heat account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應。這個失效與「凝固潛熱帳」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查冷卻曲線平台，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. This failure and a measurement bias in Solidification latent-heat account can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check a plateau in the cooling trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用冷卻曲線平台作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應。這個失效與「凝固潛熱帳」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查冷卻曲線平台，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. This failure and a measurement bias in Solidification latent-heat account can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check a plateau in the cooling trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「凝固潛熱帳」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Solidification latent-heat account\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b342-v16-13","title":"體積收縮量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Volume-shrinkage estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「體積收縮量」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Volume-shrinkage estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"總收縮量不能單獨決定縮孔位置，補縮路徑與冷卻次序也重要。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.4 cm3。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。體積收縮率是明列的整體假設；結果不決定縮孔位置。使用內部孔隙分布作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「體積收縮量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total shrinkage does not determine pore location; feeding paths and cooling order matter. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 26.4 cm3. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Volumetric shrinkage fraction is an explicit bulk assumption; the result does not locate shrinkage voids. Use distribution of internal voids as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Volume-shrinkage estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1；y=V*frac=24 cm3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1; y=V*frac=24 cm3.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「體積收縮量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Volume-shrinkage estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-13-k1","title":"體積收縮量","titleEn":"Volume-shrinkage estimate","text":"總收縮量不能單獨決定縮孔位置，補縮路徑與冷卻次序也重要。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 26.4 cm3。","textEn":"Total shrinkage does not determine pore location; feeding paths and cooling order matter. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「體積收縮量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Volume-shrinkage estimate\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷","總收縮量不能單獨決定縮孔位置，補縮路徑與冷卻次序也重要。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect.","Total shrinkage does not determine pore location; feeding paths and cooling order matter.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總收縮量不能單獨決定縮孔位置，補縮路徑與冷卻次序也重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total shrinkage does not determine pore location; feeding paths and cooling order matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b342-v16-14","title":"體積收縮量：定量估算","titleEn":"Volume-shrinkage estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「體積收縮量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Volume-shrinkage estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1；y=V*frac=24 cm3。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=26.4 cm3。模型邊界：體積收縮率是明列的整體假設；結果不決定縮孔位置；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1; y=V*frac=24 cm3. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.4 cm3. Boundary: Volumetric shrinkage fraction is an explicit bulk assumption; the result does not locate shrinkage voids; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以內部孔隙分布區分模型與觀察，先用模型凝固前後體積、內部缺陷影像及補縮路徑圖建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use distribution of internal voids to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1；y=V*frac=24 cm3。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=26.4 cm3。模型邊界：體積收縮率是明列的整體假設；結果不決定縮孔位置；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1; y=V*frac=24 cm3. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=26.4 cm3. Boundary: Volumetric shrinkage fraction is an explicit bulk assumption; the result does not locate shrinkage voids; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「體積收縮量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Volume-shrinkage estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1；y=V*frac=24 cm3。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1; y=V*frac=24 cm3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1；y=V*frac=24 cm3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=800 cm3, frac=0.03 1; y=V*frac=24 cm3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b342-v16-15","title":"體積收縮量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Volume-shrinkage estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「體積收縮量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Volume-shrinkage estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以內部孔隙分布區分模型與觀察，先用模型凝固前後體積、內部缺陷影像及補縮路徑圖建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「體積收縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use distribution of internal voids to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model before-after volumes, internal-defect images and feeding-path diagram, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Volume-shrinkage estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「體積收縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出體積收縮率是明列的整體假設；結果不決定縮孔位置如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷造成偏離的合成觀察，以內部孔隙分布說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Volume-shrinkage estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Volumetric shrinkage fraction is an explicit bulk assumption; the result does not locate shrinkage voids. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. Explain which evidence in distribution of internal voids distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以內部孔隙分布區分模型與觀察，先用模型凝固前後體積、內部缺陷影像及補縮路徑圖建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「體積收縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use distribution of internal voids to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model before-after volumes, internal-defect images and feeding-path diagram, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Volume-shrinkage estimate. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「體積收縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出體積收縮率是明列的整體假設；結果不決定縮孔位置如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷造成偏離的合成觀察，以內部孔隙分布說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Volume-shrinkage estimate, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Volumetric shrinkage fraction is an explicit bulk assumption; the result does not locate shrinkage voids. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. Explain which evidence in distribution of internal voids distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「體積收縮量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Volume-shrinkage estimate\"?","options":["本單元以內部孔隙分布區分模型與觀察，先用模型凝固前後體積、內部缺陷影像及補縮路徑圖建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量"],"optionsEn":["Use distribution of internal voids to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以內部孔隙分布區分模型與觀察，先用模型凝固前後體積、內部缺陷影像及補縮路徑圖建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use distribution of internal voids to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b342-v16-16","title":"體積收縮量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Volume-shrinkage estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「體積收縮量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Volume-shrinkage estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷。這個失效與「體積收縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查內部孔隙分布，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. This failure and a measurement bias in Volume-shrinkage estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check distribution of internal voids rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用內部孔隙分布作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷。這個失效與「體積收縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查內部孔隙分布，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. This failure and a measurement bias in Volume-shrinkage estimate can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check distribution of internal voids rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「體積收縮量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Volume-shrinkage estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b342-v16-s3","title":"線性熱收縮量與等效導熱通量","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction & Equivalent conductive heat flux","description":"本階段聚焦「線性熱收縮量」與「等效導熱通量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Linear thermal contraction\" and \"Equivalent conductive heat flux\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b342-v16-17","title":"線性熱收縮量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「線性熱收縮量」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Linear thermal contraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固態冷卻收縮與凝固體積收縮屬不同階段。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.1584 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。只算凝固完成後的自由固態收縮；不包含凝固體積收縮。使用降溫後幾何變化作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「線性熱收縮量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Solid-state thermal contraction and solidification shrinkage occur in different stages. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.1584 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Only free solid-state contraction after solidification is included; solidification volume shrinkage is excluded. Use geometry change after cooling as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Linear thermal contraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「線性熱收縮量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Linear thermal contraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-17-k1","title":"線性熱收縮量","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction","text":"固態冷卻收縮與凝固體積收縮屬不同階段。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.1584 mm。","textEn":"Solid-state thermal contraction and solidification shrinkage occur in different stages. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線性熱收縮量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Linear thermal contraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","固態冷卻收縮與凝固體積收縮屬不同階段。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","Solid-state thermal contraction and solidification shrinkage occur in different stages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固態冷卻收縮與凝固體積收縮屬不同階段。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Solid-state thermal contraction and solidification shrinkage occur in different stages. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b342-v16-18","title":"線性熱收縮量：定量估算","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「線性熱收縮量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Linear thermal contraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.1584 mm。模型邊界：只算凝固完成後的自由固態收縮；不包含凝固體積收縮；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.1584 mm. Boundary: Only free solid-state contraction after solidification is included; solidification volume shrinkage is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以降溫後幾何變化區分模型與觀察，先用同一標距的冷卻溫度與端點尺寸變化建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use geometry change after cooling to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.1584 mm。模型邊界：只算凝固完成後的自由固態收縮；不包含凝固體積收縮；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.1584 mm. Boundary: Only free solid-state contraction after solidification is included; solidification volume shrinkage is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「線性熱收縮量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Linear thermal contraction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000012 1/K, L=40 mm, dT=300 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.144 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b342-v16-19","title":"線性熱收縮量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「線性熱收縮量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Linear thermal contraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以降溫後幾何變化區分模型與觀察，先用同一標距的冷卻溫度與端點尺寸變化建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「線性熱收縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use geometry change after cooling to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cooling temperature and endpoint dimensional change over the same gauge length, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Linear thermal contraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「線性熱收縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只算凝固完成後的自由固態收縮；不包含凝固體積收縮如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以降溫後幾何變化說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Linear thermal contraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only free solid-state contraction after solidification is included; solidification volume shrinkage is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. Explain which evidence in geometry change after cooling distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以降溫後幾何變化區分模型與觀察，先用同一標距的冷卻溫度與端點尺寸變化建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「線性熱收縮量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use geometry change after cooling to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using cooling temperature and endpoint dimensional change over the same gauge length, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Linear thermal contraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「線性熱收縮量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只算凝固完成後的自由固態收縮；不包含凝固體積收縮如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以降溫後幾何變化說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Linear thermal contraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only free solid-state contraction after solidification is included; solidification volume shrinkage is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. Explain which evidence in geometry change after cooling distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「線性熱收縮量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Linear thermal contraction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以降溫後幾何變化區分模型與觀察，先用同一標距的冷卻溫度與端點尺寸變化建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use geometry change after cooling to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以降溫後幾何變化區分模型與觀察，先用同一標距的冷卻溫度與端點尺寸變化建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use geometry change after cooling to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b342-v16-20","title":"線性熱收縮量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Linear thermal contraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「線性熱收縮量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Linear thermal contraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移。這個失效與「線性熱收縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查降溫後幾何變化，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Linear thermal contraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check geometry change after cooling rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用降溫後幾何變化作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移。這個失效與「線性熱收縮量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查降溫後幾何變化，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Linear thermal contraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check geometry change after cooling rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「線性熱收縮量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Linear thermal contraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b342-v16-21","title":"等效導熱通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Equivalent conductive heat flux: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「等效導熱通量」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Equivalent conductive heat flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"一維熱流與溫度梯度成正比，有限接頭不是永久穩態。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 154000 W/m2。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。一維、定導熱係數及瞬時線性溫度梯度；不是完整暫態冷卻解。使用多位置溫度差作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「等效導熱通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"One-dimensional heat flux scales with temperature gradient, but a finite joint is not permanently steady. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 154000 W/m2. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. One-dimensional flow with constant conductivity and an instantaneous linear gradient; not a full transient cooling solution. Use temperature differences at several positions as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equivalent conductive heat flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m；y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m; y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「等效導熱通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equivalent conductive heat flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-21-k1","title":"等效導熱通量","titleEn":"Equivalent conductive heat flux","text":"一維熱流與溫度梯度成正比，有限接頭不是永久穩態。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 154000 W/m2。","textEn":"One-dimensional heat flux scales with temperature gradient, but a finite joint is not permanently steady. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「等效導熱通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Equivalent conductive heat flux\" is correct?","options":["一維熱流與溫度梯度成正比，有限接頭不是永久穩態。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔"],"optionsEn":["One-dimensional heat flux scales with temperature gradient, but a finite joint is not permanently steady.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一維熱流與溫度梯度成正比，有限接頭不是永久穩態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"One-dimensional heat flux scales with temperature gradient, but a finite joint is not permanently steady. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b342-v16-22","title":"等效導熱通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Equivalent conductive heat flux: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「等效導熱通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Equivalent conductive heat flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m；y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=154000 W/m2。模型邊界：一維、定導熱係數及瞬時線性溫度梯度；不是完整暫態冷卻解；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m; y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=154000 W/m2. Boundary: One-dimensional flow with constant conductivity and an instantaneous linear gradient; not a full transient cooling solution; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以多位置溫度差區分模型與觀察，先用模型多點溫度、測點距離及獨立熱流估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use temperature differences at several positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m；y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=154000 W/m2。模型邊界：一維、定導熱係數及瞬時線性溫度梯度；不是完整暫態冷卻解；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m; y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=154000 W/m2. Boundary: One-dimensional flow with constant conductivity and an instantaneous linear gradient; not a full transient cooling solution; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「等效導熱通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Equivalent conductive heat flux\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m；y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m; y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m；y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=35 W/mK, dT=200 K, L=0.05 m; y=k*dT/L=140000 W/m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b342-v16-23","title":"等效導熱通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Equivalent conductive heat flux: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「等效導熱通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Equivalent conductive heat flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以多位置溫度差區分模型與觀察，先用模型多點溫度、測點距離及獨立熱流估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「等效導熱通量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use temperature differences at several positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model distributed temperature, sensing-point distances and independent heat-flux estimate, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equivalent conductive heat flux. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「等效導熱通量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出一維、定導熱係數及瞬時線性溫度梯度；不是完整暫態冷卻解如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真造成偏離的合成觀察，以多位置溫度差說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equivalent conductive heat flux, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One-dimensional flow with constant conductivity and an instantaneous linear gradient; not a full transient cooling solution. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. Explain which evidence in temperature differences at several positions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以多位置溫度差區分模型與觀察，先用模型多點溫度、測點距離及獨立熱流估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「等效導熱通量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use temperature differences at several positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model distributed temperature, sensing-point distances and independent heat-flux estimate, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Equivalent conductive heat flux. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「等效導熱通量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出一維、定導熱係數及瞬時線性溫度梯度；不是完整暫態冷卻解如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真造成偏離的合成觀察，以多位置溫度差說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Equivalent conductive heat flux, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: One-dimensional flow with constant conductivity and an instantaneous linear gradient; not a full transient cooling solution. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. Explain which evidence in temperature differences at several positions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「等效導熱通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Equivalent conductive heat flux\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應","本單元以多位置溫度差區分模型與觀察，先用模型多點溫度、測點距離及獨立熱流估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","Use temperature differences at several positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以多位置溫度差區分模型與觀察，先用模型多點溫度、測點距離及獨立熱流估計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use temperature differences at several positions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b342-v16-24","title":"等效導熱通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Equivalent conductive heat flux: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「等效導熱通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equivalent conductive heat flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真。這個失效與「等效導熱通量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多位置溫度差，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Equivalent conductive heat flux can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature differences at several positions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用多位置溫度差作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真。這個失效與「等效導熱通量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多位置溫度差，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. This failure and a measurement bias in Equivalent conductive heat flux can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature differences at several positions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「等效導熱通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Equivalent conductive heat flux\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔"],"optionsEn":["Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b342-v16-s4","title":"孔隙面積比例與有效斷面應力","titleEn":"Void area fraction & Effective-section stress","description":"本階段聚焦「孔隙面積比例」與「有效斷面應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Void area fraction\" and \"Effective-section stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b342-v16-25","title":"孔隙面積比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Void area fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「孔隙面積比例」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Void area fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"切片孔隙面積率不能直接當作三維缺陷體積率。本模型把 avoid 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。分子與分母取自同一切面；不能直接推算三維體積率。使用多切面或不同聲束觀察作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一切面可能避開主要縮孔，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔隙面積比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A section void-area fraction is not directly a three-dimensional void-volume fraction. In this model, avoid is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.65 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Numerator and denominator use one section; a three-dimensional volume fraction is not directly inferred. Use multiple sections or different beam views as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. One section can miss the main shrinkage void; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Void area fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2；y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2; y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔隙面積比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Void area fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-25-k1","title":"孔隙面積比例","titleEn":"Void area fraction","text":"切片孔隙面積率不能直接當作三維缺陷體積率。本模型把 avoid 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 percent。","textEn":"A section void-area fraction is not directly a three-dimensional void-volume fraction. In this model, avoid is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔隙面積比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Void area fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔","切片孔隙面積率不能直接當作三維缺陷體積率。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void.","A section void-area fraction is not directly a three-dimensional void-volume fraction.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"切片孔隙面積率不能直接當作三維缺陷體積率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A section void-area fraction is not directly a three-dimensional void-volume fraction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b342-v16-26","title":"孔隙面積比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Void area fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔隙面積比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Void area fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2；y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent。只把 avoid 增加百分之十，y=1.65 percent。模型邊界：分子與分母取自同一切面；不能直接推算三維體積率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2; y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent. Increasing only avoid with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 percent. Boundary: Numerator and denominator use one section; a three-dimensional volume fraction is not directly inferred; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以多切面或不同聲束觀察區分模型與觀察，先用多方向切片影像、像素尺度及孔隙分割紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multiple sections or different beam views to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2；y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent。只把 avoid 增加百分之十，y=1.65 percent。模型邊界：分子與分母取自同一切面；不能直接推算三維體積率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2; y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent. Increasing only avoid with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 percent. Boundary: Numerator and denominator use one section; a three-dimensional volume fraction is not directly inferred; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔隙面積比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Void area fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2；y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2; y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2；y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: avoid=12 mm2, area=800 mm2; y=avoid/area*100=1.5 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b342-v16-27","title":"孔隙面積比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Void area fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔隙面積比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Void area fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以多切面或不同聲束觀察區分模型與觀察，先用多方向切片影像、像素尺度及孔隙分割紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「孔隙面積比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multiple sections or different beam views to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using section images in several orientations, pixel calibration and void-segmentation records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Void area fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「孔隙面積比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出分子與分母取自同一切面；不能直接推算三維體積率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一切面可能避開主要縮孔造成偏離的合成觀察，以多切面或不同聲束觀察說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Void area fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Numerator and denominator use one section; a three-dimensional volume fraction is not directly inferred. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void. Explain which evidence in multiple sections or different beam views distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One section can miss the main shrinkage void. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以多切面或不同聲束觀察區分模型與觀察，先用多方向切片影像、像素尺度及孔隙分割紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「孔隙面積比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use multiple sections or different beam views to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using section images in several orientations, pixel calibration and void-segmentation records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Void area fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「孔隙面積比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出分子與分母取自同一切面；不能直接推算三維體積率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一切面可能避開主要縮孔造成偏離的合成觀察，以多切面或不同聲束觀察說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Void area fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Numerator and denominator use one section; a three-dimensional volume fraction is not directly inferred. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void. Explain which evidence in multiple sections or different beam views distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔隙面積比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Void area fraction\"?","options":["本單元以多切面或不同聲束觀察區分模型與觀察，先用多方向切片影像、像素尺度及孔隙分割紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Use multiple sections or different beam views to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以多切面或不同聲束觀察區分模型與觀察，先用多方向切片影像、像素尺度及孔隙分割紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multiple sections or different beam views to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b342-v16-28","title":"孔隙面積比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Void area fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔隙面積比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Void area fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一切面可能避開主要縮孔。這個失效與「孔隙面積比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多切面或不同聲束觀察，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One section can miss the main shrinkage void. This failure and a measurement bias in Void area fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check multiple sections or different beam views rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用多切面或不同聲束觀察作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一切面可能避開主要縮孔，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One section can miss the main shrinkage void; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一切面可能避開主要縮孔。這個失效與「孔隙面積比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查多切面或不同聲束觀察，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"One section can miss the main shrinkage void. This failure and a measurement bias in Void area fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check multiple sections or different beam views rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔隙面積比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Void area fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","單一切面可能避開主要縮孔。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One section can miss the main shrinkage void.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一切面可能避開主要縮孔。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One section can miss the main shrinkage void. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b342-v16-29","title":"有效斷面應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective-section stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「有效斷面應力」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective-section stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淨截面應力只描述平均量，不包含缺陷尖端應力集中。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 MPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。只處理軸向淨截面平均應力；忽略缺陷尖端應力集中。使用缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效斷面應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Net-section stress describes an average and excludes defect-tip concentration. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 44 MPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Only axial net-section average stress is included; defect-tip stress concentration is excluded. Use defect dimensions and axial load as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A small-area crack can still generate high local stress; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective-section stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2；y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2; y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效斷面應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective-section stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-29-k1","title":"有效斷面應力","titleEn":"Effective-section stress","text":"淨截面應力只描述平均量，不包含缺陷尖端應力集中。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 MPa。","textEn":"Net-section stress describes an average and excludes defect-tip concentration. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效斷面應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective-section stress\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振","淨截面應力只描述平均量，不包含缺陷尖端應力集中。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","Net-section stress describes an average and excludes defect-tip concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"淨截面應力只描述平均量，不包含缺陷尖端應力集中。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Net-section stress describes an average and excludes defect-tip concentration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b342-v16-30","title":"有效斷面應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective-section stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效斷面應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective-section stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2；y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=44 MPa。模型邊界：只處理軸向淨截面平均應力；忽略缺陷尖端應力集中；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2; y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 MPa. Boundary: Only axial net-section average stress is included; defect-tip stress concentration is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷、同截面缺陷幾何及周圍應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use defect dimensions and axial load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2；y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=44 MPa。模型邊界：只處理軸向淨截面平均應力；忽略缺陷尖端應力集中；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2; y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 MPa. Boundary: Only axial net-section average stress is included; defect-tip stress concentration is excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效斷面應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective-section stress\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2；y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2; y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2；y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=300 kN, A=7600 mm2, lost=100 mm2; y=F*1000/(A-lost)=40 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b342-v16-31","title":"有效斷面應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective-section stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效斷面應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective-section stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷、同截面缺陷幾何及周圍應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「有效斷面應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use defect dimensions and axial load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic load, defect geometry on the same section and surrounding strain, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Effective-section stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「有效斷面應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只處理軸向淨截面平均應力；忽略缺陷尖端應力集中如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力造成偏離的合成觀察，以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Effective-section stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only axial net-section average stress is included; defect-tip stress concentration is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. Explain which evidence in defect dimensions and axial load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷、同截面缺陷幾何及周圍應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「有效斷面應力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use defect dimensions and axial load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic load, defect geometry on the same section and surrounding strain, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Effective-section stress. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「有效斷面應力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出只處理軸向淨截面平均應力；忽略缺陷尖端應力集中如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力造成偏離的合成觀察，以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Effective-section stress, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Only axial net-section average stress is included; defect-tip stress concentration is excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. Explain which evidence in defect dimensions and axial load distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效斷面應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective-section stress\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷、同截面缺陷幾何及周圍應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use defect dimensions and axial load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷、同截面缺陷幾何及周圍應變建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use defect dimensions and axial load to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b342-v16-32","title":"有效斷面應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective-section stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效斷面應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective-section stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力。這個失效與「有效斷面應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. This failure and a measurement bias in Effective-section stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check defect dimensions and axial load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A small-area crack can still generate high local stress.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力。這個失效與「有效斷面應力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查缺陷尺寸與軸向載荷，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. This failure and a measurement bias in Effective-section stress can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check defect dimensions and axial load rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效斷面應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective-section stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振","小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","A small-area crack can still generate high local stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小面積裂紋仍可能產生高局部應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A small-area crack can still generate high local stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b342-v16-s5","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度與檢測掃描間距","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope & Inspection scan spacing","description":"本階段聚焦「焊頂輪廓坡度」與「檢測掃描間距」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Weld crown profile slope\" and \"Inspection scan spacing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b342-v16-33","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「焊頂輪廓坡度」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Weld crown profile slope” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"輪廓斜率將表面高差和過渡長度連結。本模型把 h 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 mrad。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。高差相對過渡長度很小；結果是幾何斜率而非輪軌衝擊力。使用接頭連續縱向掃描作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「焊頂輪廓坡度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Profile slope links surface height difference with transition length. In this model, h is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 2.2 mrad. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Height difference is small relative to transition length; the result is geometric slope rather than wheel impact force. Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Weld crown profile slope” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm；y=h/L*1000=2 mrad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm; y=h/L*1000=2 mrad.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「焊頂輪廓坡度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Weld crown profile slope”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-33-k1","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope","text":"輪廓斜率將表面高差和過渡長度連結。本模型把 h 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 mrad。","textEn":"Profile slope links surface height difference with transition length. In this model, h is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焊頂輪廓坡度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Weld crown profile slope\" is correct?","options":["輪廓斜率將表面高差和過渡長度連結。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符"],"optionsEn":["Profile slope links surface height difference with transition length.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"輪廓斜率將表面高差和過渡長度連結。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Profile slope links surface height difference with transition length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b342-v16-34","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度：定量估算","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「焊頂輪廓坡度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Weld crown profile slope” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm；y=h/L*1000=2 mrad。只把 h 增加百分之十，y=2.2 mrad。模型邊界：高差相對過渡長度很小；結果是幾何斜率而非輪軌衝擊力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm; y=h/L*1000=2 mrad. Increasing only h with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 mrad. Boundary: Height difference is small relative to transition length; the result is geometric slope rather than wheel impact force; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以接頭連續縱向掃描區分模型與觀察，先用連續輪廓掃描、標距及重複掃描的定位誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm；y=h/L*1000=2 mrad。只把 h 增加百分之十，y=2.2 mrad。模型邊界：高差相對過渡長度很小；結果是幾何斜率而非輪軌衝擊力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm; y=h/L*1000=2 mrad. Increasing only h with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 mrad. Boundary: Height difference is small relative to transition length; the result is geometric slope rather than wheel impact force; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「焊頂輪廓坡度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Weld crown profile slope\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略潛熱會誤判冷卻時間","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm；y=h/L*1000=2 mrad。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：冷卻不均可能把收縮集中成缺陷"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Omitting latent heat misjudges cooling duration.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm; y=h/L*1000=2 mrad.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Uneven cooling can concentrate shrinkage into a defect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm；y=h/L*1000=2 mrad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: h=0.2 mm, L=100 mm; y=h/L*1000=2 mrad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b342-v16-35","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「焊頂輪廓坡度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Weld crown profile slope” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以接頭連續縱向掃描區分模型與觀察，先用連續輪廓掃描、標距及重複掃描的定位誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「焊頂輪廓坡度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using continuous profile scan, gauge length and repeat-scan registration error, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Weld crown profile slope. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「焊頂輪廓坡度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出高差相對過渡長度很小；結果是幾何斜率而非輪軌衝擊力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振造成偏離的合成觀察，以接頭連續縱向掃描說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Weld crown profile slope, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Height difference is small relative to transition length; the result is geometric slope rather than wheel impact force. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. Explain which evidence in continuous longitudinal scans across the joint distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以接頭連續縱向掃描區分模型與觀察，先用連續輪廓掃描、標距及重複掃描的定位誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「焊頂輪廓坡度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using continuous profile scan, gauge length and repeat-scan registration error, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Weld crown profile slope. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「焊頂輪廓坡度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出高差相對過渡長度很小；結果是幾何斜率而非輪軌衝擊力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振造成偏離的合成觀察，以接頭連續縱向掃描說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Weld crown profile slope, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Height difference is small relative to transition length; the result is geometric slope rather than wheel impact force. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. Explain which evidence in continuous longitudinal scans across the joint distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「焊頂輪廓坡度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Weld crown profile slope\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：用穩態熱流外推全部冷卻過程會失真","本單元以接頭連續縱向掃描區分模型與觀察，先用連續輪廓掃描、標距及重複掃描的定位誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Extending a steady flux over the entire cooling history distorts energy.","Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以接頭連續縱向掃描區分模型與觀察，先用連續輪廓掃描、標距及重複掃描的定位誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use continuous longitudinal scans across the joint to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b342-v16-36","title":"焊頂輪廓坡度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Weld crown profile slope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「焊頂輪廓坡度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Weld crown profile slope” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振。這個失效與「焊頂輪廓坡度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接頭連續縱向掃描，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. This failure and a measurement bias in Weld crown profile slope can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check continuous longitudinal scans across the joint rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用接頭連續縱向掃描作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振。這個失效與「焊頂輪廓坡度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接頭連續縱向掃描，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. This failure and a measurement bias in Weld crown profile slope can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check continuous longitudinal scans across the joint rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊頂輪廓坡度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Weld crown profile slope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符"],"optionsEn":["The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同高差在更短距離內形成更尖銳激振。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The same height difference over a shorter distance creates sharper excitation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b342-v16-37","title":"檢測掃描間距：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Inspection scan spacing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「檢測掃描間距」如何影響鋼軌鋁熱焊接的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inspection scan spacing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aluminothermic rail welding”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"掃描速度除量測頻率給出沿程點距，細點距仍不保證可檢出。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.55 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。速度與取樣率恆定且時間同步；不含聲束寬度及漏測。使用編碼器與取樣時間戳作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「檢測掃描間距」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Scan speed divided by acquisition rate gives spatial spacing, though fine spacing alone does not guarantee detection. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.55 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Speed and sampling rate are constant and synchronized; beam width and missed acquisitions are excluded. Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Inspection scan spacing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz；y=v/f=0.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz; y=v/f=0.5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「檢測掃描間距」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Inspection scan spacing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-37-k1","title":"檢測掃描間距","titleEn":"Inspection scan spacing","text":"掃描速度除量測頻率給出沿程點距，細點距仍不保證可檢出。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.55 mm。","textEn":"Scan speed divided by acquisition rate gives spatial spacing, though fine spacing alone does not guarantee detection. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「檢測掃描間距」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Inspection scan spacing\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符","掃描速度除量測頻率給出沿程點距，細點距仍不保證可檢出。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.","Scan speed divided by acquisition rate gives spatial spacing, though fine spacing alone does not guarantee detection.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"掃描速度除量測頻率給出沿程點距，細點距仍不保證可檢出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Scan speed divided by acquisition rate gives spatial spacing, though fine spacing alone does not guarantee detection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b342-v16-38","title":"檢測掃描間距：定量估算","titleEn":"Inspection scan spacing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「檢測掃描間距」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inspection scan spacing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz；y=v/f=0.5 mm。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.55 mm。模型邊界：速度與取樣率恆定且時間同步；不含聲束寬度及漏測；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz; y=v/f=0.5 mm. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.55 mm. Boundary: Speed and sampling rate are constant and synchronized; beam width and missed acquisitions are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以編碼器與取樣時間戳區分模型與觀察，先用編碼器位置、逐點時間戳與實際取得資料的點數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz；y=v/f=0.5 mm。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.55 mm。模型邊界：速度與取樣率恆定且時間同步；不含聲束寬度及漏測；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz; y=v/f=0.5 mm. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.55 mm. Boundary: Speed and sampling rate are constant and synchronized; beam width and missed acquisitions are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「檢測掃描間距」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Inspection scan spacing\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把平台當成感測器故障會漏掉相變效應","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把兩種收縮重複相加會高估位移","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz；y=v/f=0.5 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Mistaking a plateau for sensor failure misses phase-change behavior.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Double counting the two shrinkage stages overestimates movement.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz; y=v/f=0.5 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz；y=v/f=0.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=50 mm/s, f=100 Hz; y=v/f=0.5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b342-v16-39","title":"檢測掃描間距：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Inspection scan spacing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「檢測掃描間距」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inspection scan spacing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以編碼器與取樣時間戳區分模型與觀察，先用編碼器位置、逐點時間戳與實際取得資料的點數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「檢測掃描間距」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using encoder positions, individual timestamps and actual acquired point counts, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Inspection scan spacing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「檢測掃描間距」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出速度與取樣率恆定且時間同步；不含聲束寬度及漏測如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符造成偏離的合成觀察，以編碼器與取樣時間戳說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Inspection scan spacing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Speed and sampling rate are constant and synchronized; beam width and missed acquisitions are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. Explain which evidence in encoder positions and sampling timestamps distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以編碼器與取樣時間戳區分模型與觀察，先用編碼器位置、逐點時間戳與實際取得資料的點數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「檢測掃描間距」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using encoder positions, individual timestamps and actual acquired point counts, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Inspection scan spacing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「檢測掃描間距」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出速度與取樣率恆定且時間同步；不含聲束寬度及漏測如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符造成偏離的合成觀察，以編碼器與取樣時間戳說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Inspection scan spacing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Speed and sampling rate are constant and synchronized; beam width and missed acquisitions are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. Explain which evidence in encoder positions and sampling timestamps distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「檢測掃描間距」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Inspection scan spacing\"?","options":["本單元以編碼器與取樣時間戳區分模型與觀察，先用編碼器位置、逐點時間戳與實際取得資料的點數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一切面可能避開主要縮孔"],"optionsEn":["Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One section can miss the main shrinkage void."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以編碼器與取樣時間戳區分模型與觀察，先用編碼器位置、逐點時間戳與實際取得資料的點數建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use encoder positions and sampling timestamps to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b342-v16-40","title":"檢測掃描間距：失效診斷","titleEn":"Inspection scan spacing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b342-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「檢測掃描間距」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inspection scan spacing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符。這個失效與「檢測掃描間距」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查編碼器與取樣時間戳，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. This failure and a measurement bias in Inspection scan spacing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check encoder positions and sampling timestamps rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用編碼器與取樣時間戳作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b342-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符。這個失效與「檢測掃描間距」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查編碼器與取樣時間戳，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. This failure and a measurement bias in Inspection scan spacing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check encoder positions and sampling timestamps rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]},{"id":"b342-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢測掃描間距」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Inspection scan spacing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：外部餘料混入有效體積會高估接頭補入量"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Including surplus in effective volume overstates useful joint fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"編碼器打滑會讓名義覆蓋與實際覆蓋不符。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Encoder slip separates nominal coverage from actual coverage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-weld","v16s-track-ultra","v16s-track-cwr","v16s-track-tsi"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b342-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b342-en.svg"}};
